<section id="article-body" class="article-body valnet-segment-Gaming" itemprop="articleBody">    



    
    
<div class="content-block-regular"><p><a href="https://screenrant.com/tag/steam/" target="_blank"><strong>Steam</strong></a> has become an absolute <a href="https://screenrant.com/steam-5-free-games-october-27-2026/" target="_blank">treasure trove of free games</a> over the years, with hundreds of titles available to download and keep without tapping your wallet. The platform's massive <a href="https://screenrant.com/steam-4-free-games-october-26/" target="_blank">free-to-play library</a> is particularly appealing to gamers on a budget, offering everything from expansive MMORPGs and competitive shooters to hidden indie gems.</p>    

                                                                                                                    
<div class="w-google-addus-btn--article-header-variants is-mobile-only w-google-addus-btn--article-in-content" data-nosnippet>
    
            <div class="w-google-addus-btn w-google-addus-btn--article-full w-google-addus-btn--article-header w-google-addus-btn--article-header-options " data-stnl="%7B%22category%22%3A%22Click%20Interactions%22%2C%22name%22%3A%22Article%20Featured%20Section%22%2C%22action%22%3A%22Add%20to%20Google%22%7D">
            <div class="btn-fab google">
                <span class="w-google-addus-btn__article-intro">
                    <span class="w-google-addus-btn__article-icon icon i-google" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <span class="w-google-addus-btn__article-divider" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <span class="w-google-addus-btn__article-title">Add <strong>ScreenRant</strong> on Google</span>
                </span>
                <span class="w-google-addus-btn__article-actions">
                    <a href="https://www.google.com/preferences/source?q=screenrant.com" class="w-google-addus-btn__article-cta" data-google-add-preferred-source data-stnl="%7B%22category%22%3A%22Click%20Interactions%22%2C%22name%22%3A%22Article%20Featured%20Section%22%2C%22action%22%3A%22Add%20to%20Google%22%7D" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                        <span class="w-google-addus-btn__article-cta-text">
                            Add<span class="w-google-addus-btn__article-cta-extra"> as Preferred Source</span>
                            <span class="icon i-arrow-1" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                        </span>
                    </a>
                                                                    <a href="https://profile.google.com/@screenrant" class="w-google-addus-btn__article-cta google-addus-follow" data-stnl="%7B%22category%22%3A%22Click%20Interactions%22%2C%22name%22%3A%22Article%20Featured%20Section%22%2C%22action%22%3A%22Add%20to%20Google%20Discover%22%7D" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
                            <span class="w-google-addus-btn__article-cta-text">
                                Follow<span class="w-google-addus-btn__article-cta-extra"> on Google Discover</span>
                                <span class="icon i-arrow-1" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                            </span>
                        </a>
                                    </span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
<!-- No AdsNinja v10 Client! --><!-- No AdsNinja v10 Client! --><p>Unfortunately, there's a pretty significant catch when it comes to <a href="https://screenrant.com/dungeons-and-dragons-meets-stardew-valley-emberville-early-access/" target="_blank">free-to-play games</a>, particularly those that rely on microtransactions and in-game purchases to operate. Pay-to-win (P2W) mechanics have become an all-too-common frustration, with some developers locking powerful items, upgrades, and the best content behind real-money purchases after hooking players with the "free-to-play" label. It's an unfortunate reality that can sour an otherwise fantastic gaming experience.</p>    <p>Fortunately, this newly released <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/4429430/Origins_Trading_Card_Game/" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank">Steam</a> title is looking to buck that trend entirely, promising absolutely no pay-to-win mechanics whatsoever. It's already garnering great feedback from players, making this completely free 9/10 gem in a somewhat overcrowded genre well worth checking out.</p>    



        <div class="display-card video large no-badge">
																			
		
		<div class="w-adsninja-video-player">
			
            <div class='an-ignore'>
                <div class='adsninja-video-player emaki-video-player emaki-video-player-ab6c622120b8edf4' id='emaki-video-player-ab6c622120b8edf4'>
                    <script>
                        window.valstream       = window.valstream || {};
                        window.valstream.queue = window.valstream.queue || [];
                        
                        window.valstream.queue.push(function(){

                            const fallbackContent = `<button class="prem-player-close">x</button>
<video class='adsninja-video-player' id='emaki_video-ab6c622120b8edf4' poster='https://static0.srcdn.com/wordpress/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/steam-hardware-trailer-thumbnail.jpg?fit=crop&w=1024&h=576' controls >
    <source src='https://video.srcdn.com/2026/10/steam-official-hardware-announcement-trailer-1792428237.mp4' type='video/mp4'>
Your browser does not support the video tag.
</video>`;
                            const fallbackToNativePlayer = function(){

                                console.warn('Failed to load AdsNinja video player.');
                                const container = document.getElementById('emaki-video-player-ab6c622120b8edf4');

                                if(!container){

                                    return;
                                }

                                container.innerHTML = fallbackContent;

                                const videoPlayerContainer = document.getElementById('emaki-video-player-ab6c622120b8edf4');

                                if(videoPlayerContainer){

                                    const videoPlayer = videoPlayerContainer.querySelector('video');

                                    if(typeof Waypoint !== 'undefined' && videoPlayer){

                                        const videoPlayerWaypoint = new Waypoint.Inview({
                                            element: videoPlayerContainer,
                                            enter: function(direction){

                                                if(direction == 'up'){

                                                    this.element.classList.remove('video-player-floating');
                                                }
                                            },
                                            entered: function(direction){

                                                if(direction == 'up'){

                                                    this.element.classList.remove('video-player-floating');
                                                }
                                            },
                                            exit: function(direction){

                                                if(direction == 'down' && !videoPlayer.paused){
                                            
                                                    this.element.classList.add('video-player-floating');
                                                }
                                            },
                                            exited: function(direction){

                                                if(direction == 'down' && !videoPlayer.paused){

                                                    this.element.classList.add('video-player-floating');
                                                }
                                            },
                                            offset: -50
                                        });
                                    }

                                    const closeButton = videoPlayerContainer.querySelector('button.prem-player-close');

                                    if(closeButton){

                                        closeButton.addEventListener('click', function(){
                                    
                                            videoPlayerContainer.classList.remove('video-player-floating');

                                            if(videoPlayer){

                                                videoPlayer.pause();
                                            }
                                        });
                                    }

                                    if(videoPlayer && typeof Waypoint !== 'undefined'){

                                        videoPlayer.addEventListener('fullscreenchange', function(){

                                            Waypoint.refreshAll();
                                        });
                                    }
                                }
                            };

                            if(!window.an || typeof window.an.monetizeVideo !== 'function'){

                                fallbackToNativePlayer();
                            }
                            else{

                                window.an.monetizeVideo(
                                    '.emaki-video-player-ab6c622120b8edf4', 
                                    JSON.parse(`{\"name\":\"Instream-InContent\",\"groupName\":\"content\"}`), 
                                    JSON.parse(`{\"trackingId\":\"in-content\",\"playlist\":[{\"title\":\"Steam - Official Hardware Announcement Trailer\",\"description\":\"\",\"length\":\"6:16\",\"mimeType\":\"video\\/mp4\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/video.srcdn.com\\/2026\\/10\\/steam-official-hardware-announcement-trailer-1792428237.mp4\",\"thumbnailLink\":\"https:\\/\\/static0.srcdn.com\\/wordpress\\/wordpress\\/wp-content\\/uploads\\/2026\\/10\\/steam-hardware-trailer-thumbnail.jpg?fit=crop&w=1024&h=576\",\"textTracks\":[{\"kind\":\"subtitles\",\"label\":\"English\",\"language\":\"en\",\"url\":\"https:\\/\\/video.srcdn.com\\/2026\\/10\\/steam-official-hardware-announcement-trailer-1792428237-1792428436.vtt\",\"default\":false}]}]}`)
                                ).catch(fallbackToNativePlayer);
                            }
                        });
                    </script>
                </div>
            </div>
        
		</div>

	</div>
<p> Having officially entered Early Access on October 27, <em>Origins Trading Card Game</em> is off to an impressive start on Steam. Developed by Koin Games, the newly released free-to-play title currently boasts a "Very Positive" rating, with 89% of its first 70 or so user reviews recommending it. That's roughly a 9/10 approval rating, although it's worth noting that this only looks at positive recommendations as opposed to a traditional review score.</p>    <p><em>Origins </em>is a competitive digital trading card game that pits players against one another in fast-paced PvP battles, with matches typically lasting around seven minutes. Unlike traditional TCGs, both players take their turns simultaneously, battling across three lanes with unique conditions. There are more than 100 rotating background locations, while the cards themselves feature reimagined versions of iconic characters like Robin Hood, Mulan, Beowulf, King Arthur, Cinderella, and even Winnie-the-Pooh (though these aren't the officially licensed Disney versions, obviously).</p>    

                                        
        
                
                                                                                
                
    <div class="valnet-gallery images-count-4 " >
                                                                        <div id="article-gallery-1-1012465030"
                data-gallery-thumbnail-id="gallery-thumbnails-1-1012465030"
                data-gallery-id="main-carousel-1-1012465030"
                data-article-gallery="article-gallery-modal-1-1012465030"
                data-gallery-lightbox="gallery-modal-1-1012465030"
                data-gallery-thumbnail-img-class="gallery-thumbnails-1-1012465030-img"
