meplay.jpg?q=49&amp;amp;fit=crop&amp;amp;w=145&amp;amp;h=85&amp;amp;dpr=2\&quot; \/&gt;&lt;\/picture&gt;&lt;\/li&gt;&lt;\/ul&gt;&lt;\/div&gt;&lt;\/section&gt;&lt;\/div&gt;&quot;';
                    </script>
                            </div>
            </div>
<p>Perhaps the biggest selling point is the developer's promise of absolutely zero pay-to-win mechanics. Every competitive card can be acquired without spending money, meaning players can't simply purchase an advantage over their opponents.</p>    <p>That said, there <em>are </em>still in-game purchases, as the game's monetization gimmick revolves around premium collectibles, including limited-edition cards with alternate artwork/styles and digitally graded cards that can be traded through the Steam Marketplace. It's an interesting approach that could make <em>Origins</em> one of the more consumer-friendly TCGs, and aims to capture the appeal of popular physical TCGs such as <em>Pokémon, Disney Lorcana, </em>or<em> Magic: The Gathering</em>.</p>    
    <script>
                    window.arrayOfEmbeds["7EFg0DN9MnI"] = {'youtube' : '&quot;&lt;iframe allow=\&quot;accelerometer; autoplay; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\&quot; allowfullscreen=\&quot;\&quot; frameborder=\&quot;0\&quot; height=\&quot;315\&quot; src=\&quot;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/embed\/7EFg0DN9MnI\&quot; width=\&quot;560\&quot;&gt;&lt;\/iframe&gt;&quot;'};
            
                            window.arrayOfEmbedScripts["youtube"] = "null";
                        </script>
    
    <div class="w-rich w-youtube" id="7EFg0DN9MnI" 
            >
            </div>
<p>Early player feedback has been encouraging, particularly from those who tried the free demo and those who were given keys for Early Access. Steam reviewer <a href="https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561198146576099/recommended/4756630" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank">CryptoGorilla</a> described the experience as <em>"very fun and addictive,"</em> drawing comparisons to <em>Marvel Snap</em>. Another reviewer, <a href="https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561199142479520/recommended/4756630" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank">EbGro</a>, praised the character designs and challenging boss encounters, while <a href="https://steamcommunity.com/id/Fallendemon420/recommended/4756630" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" target="_blank">FallenDemon</a> enjoyed the gameplay but was skeptical about whether the no-P2W promise would hold up.</p>    <p>Of course, it's still extremely early, and the overwhelmingly positive reception should be taken with a grain of salt. The Early Access version has only been available for a day, meaning its relatively small pool of reviews may not accurately represent the long-term experience. Some of the more detailed player impressions also concern the earlier demo, rather than the latest release.</p>    

                
<p>Another important consideration is the game's use of AI. Koin Games has included the following disclosure on Steam:</p>    <blockquote>
                        <p>"All card art, UI, writing, and audio are created by our team. AI-assisted tools are used internally for workflow tasks and temporary placeholders only. Non-English text in the game is translated with AI from our English writing. We believe an AI-assisted translation serves players better than English-only, and we improve it as we go. The game does not generate content with AI at runtime."</p>    
            </blockquote><p>The developers additionally acknowledge using AI-assisted images in some of the cinematic trailers, although they maintain that none of this footage appears in the actual game.</p>    <p>For now, <em>Origins Trading Card Game</em> is completely free to download and play on <strong>Steam</strong>, with developers promising it will remain free-to-play even after its full 1.0 launch, currently targeted for March 2027.</p>    



        
    
                
                                
    
                            
    
                    
                    
    

        

    

        
                    
    
                                                            
